{{!-- The control for one roll of a Seasons Change move that MOVES Surplus.

      Two things roll one: a step of its own — winter's opening 1d4+Population, summer's 1d4-1,
      autumn's 1d4 at the harvest — and a result row of the move's own roll, which is winter's 7-9
      and 6- consuming another 1d4+Population. They are the same roll made in two places, so they are
      one control: the same dice, the same record of what it did, the same offer to give it back.

      Context is whichever of the two it belongs to — a SeasonStepSnapshot or a SeasonTierSnapshot.
      Both answer where they are (`address`), what they roll (`roll`), and what they have already
      done (`applied`), so nothing here asks which it was handed. Passed WITHOUT hash params: a
      partial invoked with hash args gets a flattened copy of its context, and both of these answer
      everything through prototype getters, every one of which is lost in that copy.

      Rolling MOVES Surplus, so once it has, this says what it did and offers to give it back rather
      than offering the roll again: a number that changed with nothing on screen to say why is worse
      than no automation at all. Every branch is edit-gated — they write.

      A step with no dice gets an Apply instead of a roll. That is the step the sheet adds in a season
      whose move generates nothing of its own, so that what the steading generates is paid where the
      season generates rather than in a list beside it. --}}
{{#with applied}}
	{{!-- Passed as CONTEXT, not hash params: prototype getters are lost in the flattened copy a
	      partial invoked with hash args gets. --}}
	{{> stonetop.steading-applied-line}}
	{{#if @root.editable}}
		<button type="button" class="steading-turn-reset"
		        data-action="revertSeasonStep" data-step="{{../address.key}}">
			{{localize "stonetop.steading.seasons.steps.applied.revert"}}
		</button>
	{{/if}}
{{else}}
	{{#if @root.editable}}
		{{#if die}}
		{{!-- Its ADDRESS and nothing else: the dice, the rating, which way it moves Surplus and what
		      the improvements do to all three are answered by the step itself, so a control that offers
		      2d6+Population in a township cannot describe one roll while the handler makes another. --}}
		<button type="button" class="steading-turn-roll is-plain"
		        data-action="rollSeasonStep" data-step="{{address.key}}">
			<i class="fas fa-dice-d6" aria-hidden="true"></i>
			{{!-- The dice, wherever they are not the ones the line above just named: the control is the
			      one place the roll this steading actually makes belongs, and it is what says the sheet
			      took the improvements at their word. Short to a verb only where the line already stated
			      the formula and nothing bent it — "Roll 1d4+Population" under "…rolls 1d4+Population"
			      is it twice.

			      The modifier is spelled out where there is one — "Roll 2d6 + Population − 2" — because
			      what the improvements come to is the whole reason this steading's winter is not the
			      one the line above describes, and the total it rolls is the Surplus that leaves. --}}
			<span>
				{{~#if roll.isAdjusted~}}
					{{#if stat}}{{#if modifierLabel}}{{localize
					            "stonetop.steading.seasons.steps.rollFormulaMod"
					            die=die stat=(localize statLabelKey) mod=modifierLabel}}{{else}}{{localize
					            "stonetop.steading.seasons.steps.rollFormula"
					            die=die stat=(localize statLabelKey)}}{{/if}}{{else}}{{#if modifierLabel}}{{localize
					            "stonetop.steading.seasons.steps.rollDiceMod"
					            die=die mod=modifierLabel}}{{else}}{{localize
					            "stonetop.steading.seasons.steps.rollDice" die=die}}{{/if}}{{/if}}
				{{~else if text~}}
					{{localize "stonetop.steading.seasons.steps.rollShort"}}
				{{~else~}}
					{{localize labelKey die=die stat=(localize statLabelKey)}}
				{{~/if~}}
			</span>
		</button>
		{{else}}
			{{!-- A step with no dice at all: the one the sheet adds for the steading's own gains, in a
			      season whose move generates nothing of its own. The amount is what those gains come
			      to, so the control states it and writes it — recorded and reverted exactly as a roll
			      is, because it is the same step minus the roll. --}}
			<button type="button" class="steading-turn-apply"
			        data-action="applySeasonStep" data-step="{{address.key}}">
				{{localize "stonetop.steading.seasons.steps.applyGains" amount=gainTotal}}
			</button>
		{{/if}}
	{{/if}}
{{/with}}
